--------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. DEFINITIONS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

"Software" — Themiz: its source code, scripts, agent and skill definitions,
documentation and any part of them.

"Rights holder" — Philipp Andreevich Zarubin.

"You" — the person or organisation using the Software.

"Individual use" — use by one natural person, on devices under that person's
control, for their own legal work, including work as a sole practitioner,
an individual entrepreneur (индивидуальный предприниматель), or an in-house
lawyer acting on their own behalf. Individual use stays individual when the
lawyer works on client matters and is paid for that work: what matters is that
one natural person is the only user.

"Organisational use" — anything else. In particular: use by or on behalf of a
legal entity; use by more than one person; installation on infrastructure of a
law firm, company or agency; use by employees or contractors in the course of
their duties; use for the benefit of an employer.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. WHAT IS FREE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

For individual use, the rights holder grants you, free of charge, a
non-exclusive, non-transferable, worldwide, revocable licence to:

  (a) run the Software on your own devices;
  (b) study and modify it for your own needs;
